cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use claude-markitdown-hook in your work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "claude-markitdown-hook"
abstract: >-
  A Claude Code plugin for cheap, honest document ingestion. It converts
  referenced PDFs and Office files to markdown and hands the assistant a pointer
  rather than the raw contents, avoiding the token cost of rendering document
  pages as images. Its distinguishing behaviour is failure honesty: the
  underlying converter exits successfully even when it extracts nothing, so the
  hook detects near-empty output and reports the conversion as failed instead of
  silently presenting an empty document as a complete one.
authors:
